# Northeast Flank Monitor: project rules

## What this project is
An open-source OSINT monitoring site for military activity on NATO's northeastern flank.
Full spec: docs/spec.md. Follow the spec. If a step is ambiguous or two requirements
conflict, ask me instead of deciding.

## Core question
"Is the regional military baseline changing?" Observe behavior, track the baseline,
compare historically. Do not predict intent.

## Rules
1. No predictive or alarmist language (UI copy, digests, sample text) unless directly
   quoted and attributed to a credible named source.
2. Every event has at least one attributed source (name, URL, type).
3. Locations and positions: publish what a source reports, with attribution to that
   source. Do not invent or infer positions that no source states.
4. Official Russian/Belarusian claims are labeled as state sources and not treated as
   independently verified.
5. Historical comparison always carries the note that similarity is not trajectory.
6. Northeast Flank Activity Index: part of the project. Build it per the spec, with the
   permanent disclaimer that it measures observable activity and is not a probability of
   conflict. Scoring formula must be documented. Build order follows the roadmap I set.
7. AI-extracted events go to a review queue first; only approved events are public.

## Engineering rules
- Work in small steps, one per prompt. Outline the plan before any step touching
  more than 3 files.
- Follow the stack and repo structure in docs/spec.md unless I say otherwise.
- Schema changes go through migrations.
- After each step: list what changed, what you did not do, and open questions.

## Design (UI steps only)
Palette and typography are in docs/spec.md sections 47-51.
